## What the patch is
A byte-exact FORWARD `git show f64a874 -- src/python/model/model.py`. It ADDS an
already-shipped, clean log-sanitization feature: imports `sanitize_log_value` from
`common` and wraps the file-name interpolation in the add_file/remove_file/
update_file debug log lines (`'{}'.format(sanitize_log_value(file.name))` etc.);
dict keys, lookups, deletions, and listener notifications stay raw by design. This
is defect-free feature code — reviewing it should produce NO critical/warning
finding. Safe ON the log-sanitization/secret-handling axis: the change strictly
REDUCES what reaches the logs; it introduces no leak, no injection, no behavior
change outside log formatting.

